**Title**: Cross-Sub-Sector Volatility Transmission and Lead-Lag Dynamics in FTSE 100 Energy

**Description**: This study quantifies risk transmission between Integrated/Utility and E&P Pure-Play sub-sectors by constructing equal-weighted indices from normalized GBP-denominated returns. To mitigate artificial variance spikes, we apply a robust filter to log returns during identified ex-dividend windows, ensuring variance estimates reflect fundamental market activity rather than discrete corporate actions. We employ a 5-day rolling window Huber M-estimator to calculate sub-sector volatility and evaluate the temporal lead-lag relationship between E&P volume intensity and Integrated/Utility volatility. By analyzing the cross-correlation of these time series, we identify regime shifts in sector-wide risk transmission. This approach isolates systematic volatility linkages without requiring missing market-capitalization data, providing a high-fidelity assessment of how liquidity-driven shocks in pure-play assets propagate to the broader energy sector.
\end{IDEA}


